WEBVTT

00:00.920 --> 00:07.592
As I stand in the wind on a hill by a port town,

00:00.920 --> 00:07.592
minatomachi oka no ue kaze wo uke

00:07.656 --> 00:14.683
mezurashii kurai atama wa karappo

00:07.656 --> 00:14.683
my head feels unusually empty.

00:15.268 --> 00:21.940
I was watching the town from the south side of the shore.

00:15.268 --> 00:21.940
haruka minami mukougishi de kono machi wo miteita

00:21.965 --> 00:28.179
And so I sunk my unsteady passion into the depths of the sea.

00:21.965 --> 00:28.179
guratsuita jounetsu wo umi ni shizumeta

00:29.073 --> 00:34.745
This surging power...

00:29.073 --> 00:34.745
tome donaku afureru chikara

00:29.073 --> 00:31.160
Black Jack

00:36.247 --> 00:42.502
It's something hidden in everyone, everywhere.

00:36.247 --> 00:42.502
sonnamono wa darenimo dokonimo hisonde iru mono

00:43.296 --> 00:48.258
Day after day, everyone tries their best.

00:43.296 --> 00:48.258
mainichi mainichi minna ganbaru

00:49.829 --> 00:57.184
But people get annoyed when I mention it.

00:49.829 --> 00:57.184
sore wo ieba hito wa mina kemutagaru

00:57.685 --> 00:59.376
Oh FREEDOM

00:59.376 --> 01:01.369
will be there

01:01.389 --> 01:04.349
It makes me glad...

01:01.389 --> 01:04.349
yokatta

01:04.594 --> 01:12.074
That I found my place here.

01:04.594 --> 01:12.074
ibasho ga koko ni attakara

01:12.127 --> 01:13.645
Oh WISDOM

01:13.645 --> 01:15.494
will be there

01:15.522 --> 01:18.163
I searched for the reason

01:15.522 --> 01:18.163
sagashita

01:18.164 --> 01:25.212
why we can believe in the same air

01:18.164 --> 01:25.212
onaji kuuki shinjirarerukoto

01:25.797 --> 01:32.677
as long as we're alive.

01:25.797 --> 01:32.677
ínochi aru kagiri

01:32.678 --> 01:34.763
He weaves the thread of life with his miraculous control of a scalpel.

01:34.847 --> 01:37.031
The genius surgeon who lives on a cape.

01:37.183 --> 01:39.794
His name is Black Jack.

01:50.590 --> 01:58.551
I want to capture your heart with my silly smile...

01:58.723 --> 02:06.816
Just look straight at me...

02:13.335 --> 02:17.366
Sheesh! Just when I swept it all up!

02:22.497 --> 02:23.664
I hate spiders!

02:23.999 --> 02:25.745
Get off!

02:29.379 --> 02:31.922
N-No! No! No! No!

02:32.002 --> 02:33.340
No!

02:36.052 --> 02:38.712
Ohmigewdness!

02:43.977 --> 02:45.310
A ¥1,000 note?

02:46.013 --> 02:48.439
Pinoco, what have you been doing?

02:48.659 --> 02:51.900
Doc, we found money.

02:53.153 --> 02:54.056
Money?

02:56.288 --> 02:59.450
Originally "The Robin & the Boy"” by Tezuka Osamu

02:56.288 --> 02:59.450
The Robin and the Boy

02:59.701 --> 03:00.743
Let's see...

03:00.744 --> 03:03.912
¥25,320.

03:04.622 --> 03:06.915
That's a mystery.

03:07.625 --> 03:10.362
Mysterious money coming to the Black Jack residence...

03:10.670 --> 03:12.838
There must be something behind this.

03:12.839 --> 03:14.798
I don't care.

03:15.077 --> 03:18.761
We have a lot of year-end expenses, so this is a great help.

03:18.762 --> 03:22.097
Girls are too pragmatic.

03:22.328 --> 03:26.560
But Doc told me not to use this money until
we find out where it's coming from.

03:26.895 --> 03:29.688
Then I'll solve the mystery!

03:29.689 --> 03:30.773
Really?

03:30.774 --> 03:32.964
Then I'll work hard at it too.

03:33.151 --> 03:36.195
The New Year's Day mochi are at stake here.

03:37.614 --> 03:39.010
Sharaku,

03:39.282 --> 03:41.659
what's that weird thing?

03:41.660 --> 03:43.577
It's the detector I designed.

03:43.578 --> 03:44.828
A detector?

03:44.829 --> 03:47.788
We can find things that are buried under the ground.

03:48.291 --> 03:51.669
Someone must have buried money around here.

03:51.670 --> 03:55.589
And that money got carried by the
wind to the Black Jack residence.

03:55.590 --> 03:57.222
That's what I've deduced.

03:58.192 --> 04:01.679
And that "someone" might be a bank robber;

04:01.912 --> 04:02.879
A robber?!

04:03.292 --> 04:06.684
This investigation might become dangerous.

04:06.685 --> 04:07.549
Dangerous?!

04:10.647 --> 04:11.814
This is the spot!

04:13.566 --> 04:14.984
A large sum of money must be here.

04:26.162 --> 04:27.705
What's this?!

04:27.706 --> 04:29.331
Oh no!

04:29.332 --> 04:32.140
The water main broke!

04:37.841 --> 04:39.466
What the heck were you doing?

04:39.467 --> 04:43.721
We were searching for the source of the money.

04:44.264 --> 04:48.007
I thought there might be some criminal behind this.

04:48.351 --> 04:49.578
Idiotic.

04:49.894 --> 04:52.094
Anyway, if you catch a cold, you...

04:56.151 --> 04:57.526
Hey, come over here!

04:58.361 --> 05:00.276
What is it, Doc?

05:00.488 --> 05:01.989
Look at that.

05:06.494 --> 05:07.619
A bird!

05:07.620 --> 05:10.539
The bird has money in its beak!

05:14.711 --> 05:16.837
That's a Japanese robin.

05:16.838 --> 05:18.005
Japanese robin?

05:18.423 --> 05:20.653
It's strange to see one at this time of year.

05:21.009 --> 05:23.970
The Japanese robin is a migratory bird, right?

05:24.346 --> 05:27.306
They're only in Japan during the summer,

05:27.307 --> 05:30.237
so it should have migrated to another country by now.

05:31.686 --> 05:34.135
I wonder why it's still around.

05:39.904 --> 05:42.690
Wait! Robin!

05:46.743 --> 05:50.954
That robin left the money.

05:51.706 --> 05:54.683
This is an even greater mystery!

06:23.071 --> 06:25.531
He brought ¥1,000 and ¥500 yesterday.

06:25.718 --> 06:27.771
And ¥300 for today.

06:27.993 --> 06:30.262
It's now over ¥50,000.

06:30.787 --> 06:34.060
It's said that robins bring happiness,

06:34.290 --> 06:36.417
but I never knew that they brought money too.

06:36.418 --> 06:39.503
| wonder why he’s bringing it to us?

06:40.839 --> 06:41.696
Should we ask him?

06:46.386 --> 06:49.596
What are you doing with that perfume?

06:49.597 --> 06:50.597
Just watch.

07:16.610 --> 07:17.150
Good!

07:43.151 --> 07:46.829
Doc, that's where the robin's nest is?

07:55.538 --> 07:58.473
Doc, there's a female bird here!

07:58.792 --> 08:01.085
Her wing is injured.

08:01.086 --> 08:01.993
Injured?

08:02.504 --> 08:06.632
Don't tell me he wanted me to treat that injury.

08:06.856 --> 08:09.051
The injury is almost healed.

08:09.052 --> 08:11.043
I think someone already treated her.

08:11.522 --> 08:13.318
There's money here too.

08:22.816 --> 08:24.316
Owie!

08:24.317 --> 08:25.317
Owie!

08:25.318 --> 08:27.509
That happens when you try to take money from a nest.

08:27.737 --> 08:29.697
Not the money.

08:29.698 --> 08:31.115
This.

08:31.700 --> 08:32.964
A medicine bottle?

08:33.711 --> 08:36.050
Yes, I remember that well.

08:36.121 --> 08:41.583
A while ago, a boy visited me with an injured wild bird.

08:44.045 --> 08:45.713
Its wing is injured.

08:46.089 --> 08:48.649
Can you make medicine to treat it?

08:49.009 --> 08:50.154
Please.

08:50.468 --> 08:55.213
I prepared the medicine for its injury.

08:55.432 --> 09:00.313
That boy treated the robin using that medicine,

09:00.645 --> 09:05.149
and he told me that its mate kept
watch from outside his window.

09:05.525 --> 09:07.484
Isn't that an adorable story?

09:11.774 --> 09:14.814
Eventually, the robins became friends with that boy,

09:15.243 --> 09:18.537
and they visited me on his shoulders.

09:20.165 --> 09:23.920
That boy was going to school while working on the side.

09:24.169 --> 09:27.421
It seems it was a stretch for him
to keep paying for the medicine,

09:27.881 --> 09:32.926
But, because of his efforts,
the robin's injury got much better.

09:32.927 --> 09:35.304
He's such a caring boy.

09:35.764 --> 09:40.851
The boy said that he was going to give
this medicine bottle to the bird.

09:41.001 --> 09:45.371
The robins probably learned the
effects of the medicine too.

09:45.690 --> 09:47.316
They're very smart.

09:49.373 --> 09:51.324
But what about it?

09:51.571 --> 09:55.240
That robin is bringing money to my place.

09:55.488 --> 09:56.348
Money?

09:56.441 --> 09:57.521
But why?

09:58.161 --> 10:00.014
We're trying to find out why.

10:02.332 --> 10:04.667
Do you know anything about that boy?

10:05.085 --> 10:07.356
He's a newspaper boy.

10:07.712 --> 10:10.172
You know, I haven't seen him lately.

10:12.252 --> 10:14.965
Machinaka
Newspaper

10:12.252 --> 10:14.965
Distributor

10:12.592 --> 10:15.143
That boy quit.

10:15.470 --> 10:16.281
Quit?

10:16.513 --> 10:21.350
He was a hard worker, but he fell ill.

10:21.411 --> 10:22.935
Where does he live?

10:23.098 --> 10:25.874
He lived here while he was working for me,

10:26.231 --> 10:28.399
but I don't know what's happened to him since he quit.

10:28.594 --> 10:29.543
How terrible!

10:29.567 --> 10:32.319
You chased him away just because he fell ill?

10:32.320 --> 10:34.238
Don't blame me!

10:34.239 --> 10:36.281
He left on his own!

10:36.741 --> 10:39.231
He said that he didn't want to cause any trouble for me.

10:39.786 --> 10:45.249
He has no family, so I'm sure he didn't go too far.

10:50.797 --> 10:53.215
A newspaper boy?

10:53.216 --> 10:55.509
I haven't seen him.

10:56.803 --> 10:58.262
Okay, let's go.

11:04.269 --> 11:06.562
He's a friend of birds.

11:06.563 --> 11:08.105
I don't know.

11:11.568 --> 11:14.987
I used to see him, but I haven't lately.

11:20.994 --> 11:22.894
We can't find him.

11:23.246 --> 11:24.945
We don't even know what he looks like.

11:25.790 --> 11:28.518
This is like trying to grab a cloud.

11:33.895 --> 11:34.669
I know!

11:34.924 --> 11:36.508
We can ask the birds!

12:02.202 --> 12:03.208
This is it!

12:17.509 --> 12:18.926
The last room, right?

12:26.101 --> 12:27.101
Excuse me.

12:35.527 --> 12:36.418
This is...

12:41.157 --> 12:42.866
Doc!

12:42.867 --> 12:44.618
It must be his kidneys.

12:46.705 --> 12:47.621
Who are you?

12:47.776 --> 12:48.706
Ahem.

12:48.707 --> 12:51.250
He's the best doctor in the world.

12:51.251 --> 12:53.544
He can cure any disease.

12:54.212 --> 12:56.260
A-A doctor?

12:56.809 --> 12:59.508
Why didn't you see a doctor sooner?

13:01.136 --> 13:02.511
I have no money.

13:02.929 --> 13:04.567
Come to my clinic right now.

13:04.931 --> 13:07.010
You'll die if we don't treat you now.

13:07.517 --> 13:10.019
But I don't have any money to pay for it.

13:11.021 --> 13:12.313
I've already received the treatment fee.

13:14.357 --> 13:15.774
From the requester.

13:38.381 --> 13:42.134
It was the beginning of summer when I found the robin.

13:54.898 --> 14:01.070
While I was delivering newspapers, I found a female
robin who was injured and struggling.

14:02.030 --> 14:07.868
I took her home and gave her medicine,
and she started to get better.

14:09.170 --> 14:13.957
So I gave her the medicine and returned her to her nest.

14:17.962 --> 14:23.776
I started to enjoy watching the robins
while I delivered newspapers.

14:25.095 --> 14:28.535
By the end of the summer,
she seemed to be much better,

14:28.973 --> 14:32.267
and showed me that she could flap her wings.

14:39.067 --> 14:42.569
But by then, I'd started to...

15:13.935 --> 15:18.522
There's ¥57,238 here.

15:20.747 --> 15:27.531
The robin gathered the money and
brought it to us day after day,

15:27.532 --> 15:29.992
even when it was windy or rainy.

15:41.838 --> 15:46.835
That robin must have known that I'm
someone who can treat illnesses.

15:47.761 --> 15:49.511
Even after the migration season,

15:50.388 --> 15:54.424
he was still concerned about you
and kept bringing me money.

16:00.815 --> 16:03.400
It's quite enough for the surgical fee.

16:03.860 --> 16:06.362
I guarantee that I will cure your illness.

16:08.281 --> 16:10.353
Let's start the operation.

16:10.700 --> 16:12.326
Pinoco, prepare the an aesthetic.

16:12.327 --> 16:14.841
Aye-aye!

16:22.808 --> 16:23.375
Clamps.

16:24.462 --> 16:25.009
Here.

17:18.476 --> 17:23.802
Doc, the robin brought money again.

17:25.066 --> 17:26.859
Tell it we don't need money anymore,

17:26.860 --> 17:29.110
and that he's fine now.

17:29.571 --> 17:31.349
Will he understand?

17:31.781 --> 17:32.658
Who knows?

17:46.504 --> 17:47.629
Money again.

17:56.526 --> 17:57.120
How dangerous!

18:06.566 --> 18:07.790
You can stop this now!

18:08.026 --> 18:09.115
You've done enough.

18:09.736 --> 18:11.395
You should rest until spring.

18:13.281 --> 18:17.451
I might be greedy, but I can't accept any more money.

18:18.036 --> 18:19.203
It's enough.

18:20.914 --> 18:22.603
You don't need to bring any more money.

18:42.426 --> 18:46.188
Then that idiot ran to the police box.

18:46.228 --> 18:47.166
Seriously?

18:47.401 --> 18:49.857
Then he got caught himself.

18:52.606 --> 18:54.143
It's carrying something.

18:54.364 --> 18:56.073
That's money!

18:57.242 --> 18:58.659
I'll take it away!

18:58.660 --> 18:59.807
Yeah! Me too!

19:12.382 --> 19:13.585
It's gone...

19:14.384 --> 19:15.316
Damn.

19:26.604 --> 19:29.262
I'll go visit the robins nest tomorrow.

19:29.566 --> 19:32.067
If I show I'm fine, they'll...

19:32.173 --> 19:34.945
The robins will feel relieved too.

19:34.946 --> 19:37.031
Here. This is your medicine.

19:41.578 --> 19:44.770
Largo! Stay quiet!

20:09.230 --> 20:12.399
The robin brought money again.

20:14.319 --> 20:17.655
Doc! Bad news!

20:17.656 --> 20:19.573
Bad news!

20:19.908 --> 20:22.034
What's the ruckus about?

20:22.035 --> 20:26.299
I found blood along with the money from the robin!

20:26.581 --> 20:27.498
What?

20:48.853 --> 20:53.941
He carried the last bit of money while enduring great pain.

20:56.903 --> 20:58.217
It's me.

20:58.488 --> 21:02.366
See? I got better because of you.

21:14.065 --> 21:16.472
Sign: "Robin's Tomb"

21:35.233 --> 21:37.443
Look, the robin is...

22:00.592 --> 22:02.676
Robin!

22:02.677 --> 22:05.183
Take care!

22:10.504 --> 22:17.510
I want to capture your heart with my silly smile.

22:10.504 --> 22:17.510
itazura no hohemi de muchuu ni sasetaino

22:17.511 --> 22:24.683
Only look straight at me.

22:17.511 --> 22:24.683
massugu na kimi no me ni watashi wo utsushitene

22:24.728 --> 22:31.985
Being kind isn't good enough.

22:24.728 --> 22:31.985
yasashii dake dewa nanika tarinaino

22:31.986 --> 22:42.495
I want to get in touch with your true heart, deep
within the you that nobody else sees.

22:31.986 --> 22:42.495
dare nimo misenai kokoro no oku no sotto furetai

22:42.496 --> 22:47.876
Being in the gentle sunlight,

22:42.496 --> 22:47.876
yawaraka na hizashi abite

22:47.877 --> 22:57.260
I wish on the clover that plays the melody of dreams,

22:47.877 --> 22:53.082
yume wo kanaderu clover

22:53.537 --> 22:57.261
kaze ni negai wo nosete

22:57.261 --> 23:08.021
and I search for a ray of hope beyond the blue skies,

22:57.261 --> 23:08.021
aoi sora no mukou e kibou no hikari sagasuno

23:08.022 --> 23:13.109
because I want to stay by your side forever.

23:08.022 --> 23:13.109
zutto soba ni itakara

23:13.110 --> 23:26.080
The promise we made long ago in a far away place...

23:13.110 --> 23:26.080
haruka kanata de zutto mae kara

23:26.081 --> 23:33.004
is finally coming to a realization, overcoming the incredible distance,

23:26.081 --> 23:33.004
hikari ni terasare michibikareru youni

23:33.005 --> 23:43.890
just as it was lead by the light.

23:33.005 --> 23:36.938
sora no hate tooku

23:37.031 --> 23:43.831
toki wo koete ima tadori tsuku

23:45.055 --> 24:15.002
The Real Desire of the Facial Deformation

23:45.741 --> 23:48.194
Something is happening inside this man's mind.

23:48.921 --> 23:50.728
It's not necessarily a lie.

23:50.849 --> 23:51.815
As long as I'm cured...

23:51.815 --> 23:54.082
It's an invisible man!

23:54.329 --> 23:57.842
One day, it came out with no warning...

23:58.068 --> 24:00.704
Because of it, I can't even go out.

24:02.422 --> 24:03.822
Doc!

24:04.543 --> 24:05.663
No way!

24:05.703 --> 24:06.903
Don't touch me.

24:07.210 --> 24:08.390
Who's talking?

24:08.590 --> 24:10.083
The other me.

24:10.790 --> 24:11.790
The other?

24:12.177 --> 24:14.628
Next Karte - The Real Desire of the Facial Deformation.

24:16.073 --> 24:17.824
Karte NG...

24:18.534 --> 24:21.244
I hate spiders!

24:22.914 --> 24:24.601
Ohmygewdness!
